 "title": "CORS",
 "sources": [
  "MDN Web Docs, 'Cross-Origin Resource Sharing (CORS)' (fetched 2026-11-17): CORS is an HTTP-header based mechanism that allows a server to indicate any origins (domain, scheme, or port) other than its own from which a browser should permit loading resources; browsers restrict cross-origin HTTP requests initiated from scripts under the same-origin policy; for preflighted requests the browser first sends an OPTIONS request to check the actual request is safe; Access-Control-Allow-Origin names a single origin, or * for requests without credentials; for credentialed requests the server must not use the * wildcard and must specify an explicit origin, otherwise the browser blocks access to the response. https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/CORS",
  "Inference from the above, not stated verbatim: because enforcement is done by browsers, a tool that is not a browser (curl, a server script) is not stopped by CORS. Postman is named as such a tool."
 ],
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Your API call works in Postman, but in the browser it fails with a CORS error. Is your server broken?",
   "caps": "WORKS IN *POSTMAN | FAILS IN THE *BROWSER | *CORS ERROR"
  },
  {
   "text": "No. CORS is a rule your browser enforces, not your server.",
   "caps": "NOT YOUR SERVER | THE *BROWSER ENFORCES IT"
  },
  {
   "text": "By default, scripts can only call the origin the page came from: same scheme, domain, and port.",
   "caps": "SAME *ORIGIN | SCHEME, *DOMAIN, PORT"
  },
  {
   "text": "To allow another origin, the server replies with an Access-Control-Allow-Origin header naming it.",
   "caps": "SERVER *REPLIES | *ALLOW-ORIGIN HEADER | NAMES THE *ORIGIN"
  },
  {
   "text": "For requests that could change data, the browser first sends a preflight, an OPTIONS request, to ask if it's safe.",
   "caps": "*PREFLIGHT | THE *OPTIONS METHOD | ASKS IF *SAFE"
  },
  {
   "text": "Postman isn't a browser, so it never enforces any of this, which is why it works there.",
   "caps": "POSTMAN IS *NOT A BROWSER | NO *ENFORCEMENT"
  },
  {
   "text": "But here's the catch: if the request sends cookies, the server can't answer with a star. The browser blocks it.",
   "caps": "BUT THERE IS A *CATCH | COOKIES SENT | NO *STAR ALLOWED"
  },
  {
   "text": "So name the exact origins you trust, and remember CORS won't stop curl or a script from calling your API.",
   "caps": "NAME *EXACT ORIGINS | CORS *DOESN'T STOP CURL"
  }
 ],
